-- title:
--   Idelic factorisation of norm-one quaternion ideles from local density
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be nonzero rationals and $B=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, and let $O$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $B$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb Q$-span is all of $B$, and it is finitely generated. Assume the following density hypothesis at every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$: if $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ contains a nonzero non-unit, then for every $s'\in B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ such that $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi(s'))=1$ for every ring isomorphism $\varphi\colon B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w\to\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{\mathrm{imI}},z_{\mathrm{imJ}},z_{\mathrm{imK}})$ coordinatewise, and for every nonzero $M\in\mathbb N$, there is $\beta\in B$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\beta)=1$ such that $\beta\otimes 1=1+M z$ at each place $w'\neq w$ and $\beta\otimes 1=s'+Mz$ at $w$, with $z$ in the local box of $O$ (the additive subgroup generated by $z_0\otimes c$ with $z_0\in O$ and $c$ a $w'$-adic, resp. $w$-adic, integer). Let $y$ be a unit of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose component at every $w$ has reduced norm $1$, in the same sense via all such $\varphi$. Then there are a unit $\beta$ of $B$ and a unit $u$ of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\beta)=1$, with $u$ stabilising the finite adelic box of $O$ under multiplication, and with $y$ equal to the image of $\beta$ under the diagonal embedding times $u$.
--
--   This is the reduction step behind strong approximation for quaternion algebras in the style of Kneser: given local density of global reduced-norm-one elements at each finite place, the norm-one finite ideles of $B$ are exhausted by global norm-one units times units stabilising $\widehat O$. It is the version with no distinguished place exempted, and feeds into [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one_of_forall_isUnit`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one_of_forall_isUnit).
-- source:
